# Changelog / Release notes

The information about Unicis Platform releases and changes is listed in order below.

TODO: change the release date
## [Fleet Server + Asset Management Module] 2026-**-**

*Release date: 2026-06-30*

- New Features
  - Fleet Server — dedicated backend for device management and osquery orchestration
    - Fleet server code kept in a private repository, shared exclusively with Ultimate plan users
    - SaaS Ultimate users order Asset Configuration via the UI interface (no manual fleet setup required)
  - Asset Management module — browse, search, filter, and inspect enrolled devices
    - Assets dashboard with per-platform breakdown (Windows, Linux, macOS) and pie chart
    - Task analysis summary (new, pending, completed, failed queries)
    - Per-asset detail pages: Overview, Status Logs, Result Logs, Asset Configurations
    - Add Asset workflow with platform-specific CLI installer instructions
    - Fleet authentication / bootstrap flow (login, password change, account creation, forgot password)
- Enhancements
  - Asset Management made responsive across mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports
    - Asset list header stacks vertically on small screens; controls wrap and search goes full-width
    - Tab navigation (asset detail tabs, platform tabs) scrolls horizontally on narrow viewports
    - Result log summary layout adjusted for better mobile fit
  - GlitchTip error tracking enabled for SaaS deployments, hosted in the EU
  - `.env.example` updated with production Fleet endpoints and token
- Fixes
  - Task attachments now correctly accept image files (PNG, JPEG) when the browser does not supply a MIME type — drag-and-drop from external sources no longer silently rejects valid images
  - Both client-side (`taskService.ts`) and server-side (`attachment.ts`) file-type validation fall back to extension check when `file.type` / `file.mimetype` is empty, while still verifying file content via magic-byte signature
## [Library updates, Compliance hardening and  Bug fixes] 2026-07-08

*Release date: 2026-07-08*

- Security & Dependency Updates
  - Patched Critical/High vulnerabilities found in a Grype scan of the SBOM: `ws`, `form-data`, `protobufjs`, `hono`, `@grpc/grpc-js`, and `i18next-fs-backend` bumped to their fixed versions
  - `xlsx` switched from the abandoned npm registry package (0.18.5, unpatched ReDoS/prototype-pollution CVEs) to SheetJS's own CDN distribution (0.20.3), which contains the actual fixes
  - `daisyUI` upgraded 5.5.19 → 5.6.13 — compiled-CSS diffed against the previous version to confirm no breaking changes to classes used in this app
  - Added [`.well-known/security.txt`](https://securitytxt.org/) with our disclosure contact, policy, and OpenBugBounty program links
  - **[SAST-02 / CWE-22]** Fixed path traversal in attachment download — filename from the database is now passed through `path.basename()` before being joined with the upload directory, preventing any stored `../` components from escaping the intended directory
  - **[SAST-03 / CWE-693]** Added `Content-Security-Policy`, `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`, and `Permissions-Policy` (camera, microphone, geolocation, interest-cohort all denied) to the global `next.config.js` headers block; `unsafe-eval` is present only in development mode (required by Next.js HMR) and omitted from production builds
  - **[SAST-04 / CWE-20]** Fixed `callbackUrl` trailing-space typo in `middleware.ts` that caused NextAuth to silently ignore the post-login redirect parameter
  - **[XSS-01 / CWE-79]** Added server-side URL protocol validation (`https:` / `http:` allowlist) to the IAP course create and update API routes, blocking `javascript:` and `data:` scheme payloads from being stored as course URLs
  - **[XSS-01 / CWE-601]** Added `sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-fullscreen"` to the IAP course content iframe, preventing sandboxed content from navigating the top frame or accessing cookies
  - **[XSS-02 / CWE-79]** `MarkdownPreview` now overrides the `a` component to rewrite any `href` that does not match `https?:`, `mailto:`, `#`, or `/` to `#`, blocking stored `javascript:` hrefs from executing in rendered markdown
  - **[Quill CVE]** Pinned `quill` to `2.0.2` (direct dependency + `overrides` entry) to block the XSS vulnerability present in `2.0.3`; the override covers transitive consumers `react-quill-new` and `quill-markdown-shortcuts`
  - Updated regulatory compliance assessment (GDPR, SOC 2, ISO 27001:2022, NIS2) — GDPR Controller score raised 52 → 58/100 reflecting the public Right to Erasure Request Form at https://handbook.unicis.tech/pub/erasure-request-form
  - Retraced audit log correctly identified as self-hosted (not external); ULTIMATE-plan-only scope documented as an intentional product decision pending future expansion
  - CSP `connect-src` comment corrected — removed stale Sentry/Mixpanel references; now accurately lists Matomo (self-hosted), GlitchTip (EU-hosted), and OVH AI endpoint
- Fixed
  - Duplicate module page titles on Risk Management, Privacy Impact Assessment, Transfer Impact Assessment, Record of Processing Activities, Interactive Awareness Training, and Cybersecurity Management System — the sticky header and each module's own dashboard were both rendering a title
  - Record of Processing Activities had two different names shown across the app ("Record of Processing Activities" vs "Register of Procedures"); unified on the former
  - Cybersecurity Management System had no record-count badge on its page heading or sidebar entry
  - All Tasks sidebar and page title now show a total task count (previously only showed a badge when tasks were overdue)
  - Task detail page had its own inline breadcrumb and title, inconsistent with every other module; now shown as "All Tasks [count] › # - Task name" in the shared header, matching the same pattern
  - TypeScript error in `components/shared/uiw/Markdown.tsx` — `safeComponents` now typed as `Components` from `react-markdown` instead of an inlined anonymous object type, resolving the TS compiler error at line 54
  - TypeScript error in `pages/api/auth/[...nextauth].ts` — `PrismaAdapter` call now casts `prisma` to the adapter's own parameter type to accommodate the custom Prisma client output path; resolves the TS compiler error at line 23 without widening to `any`
  - `next-env.d.ts` route type reference updated from `.next/dev/types/routes.d.ts` to `.next/types/routes.d.ts` (production build path)
  - Fix due date in EU style DD/MM/YYYY
- Enhancements
  - Module title and record-count badge moved out of each module's content area and into the shared sticky header, positioned to the left of the search field, for RPA, TIA, PIA, RM, IAP, and CSC — frees a full row of vertical space on every module page
  - Settings sub-pages (Settings, Billing, Members, Training, Single Sign-On, Directory Sync, Audit Logs, Webhooks, API Keys) now show "Settings: {team name}" in the header instead of repeating the team name as an in-content heading on every tab
  - Cybersecurity Management System's record count reflects only the currently selected framework tab; the tab selection is now synced to the URL (`?framework=`), making a specific framework tab deep-linkable and bookmarkable
  - Sidebar navigation gained a neutral (grey) "total items" badge for Record of Processing Activities, Transfer Impact Assessment, Privacy Impact Assessment, and Interactive Awareness Training, alongside the existing red/amber "needs attention" badges on Tasks, Risk Management, and Cybersecurity Management System
  - Added a [Weblate translation status badge](https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/unicis-platform/) to the README

## [MCP Server, Analytics & Error Tracking] 2026-06-30

*Release date: 2026-06-29*

- New Features
  - **MCP Server merged into this repository** — the [Unicis MCP Server](src/mcp-server) is no longer a separate companion repo; its source now lives at `src/mcp-server` as a self-contained Node.js package (own `package.json`/`tsconfig.json`, talks to the platform over its public REST API)
  - **GlitchTip error tracking** — client/server/edge Sentry SDK configs wired against a single GlitchTip project, tagging events with `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV` (local/dev/prod) instead of `NODE_ENV` since both deployed environments run in production mode
  - **Matomo content & event tracking** — page/content tracking on the pricing page plus broader event instrumentation across the app (e.g. first framework selection on the activation funnel)
  - **Image upload support for attachments** — task attachments now accept PNG/JPEG with server-side magic-byte validation
- Fixed
  - Attachment upload error handling — localized error messages across all 7 supported languages; notification failures no longer affect file-save success/error reporting
  - README hero logo/banner image reference corrected

## [UX/UI Redesign, Dashboard & Accessibility] 2026-06-12

*Release date: 2026-06-12*

- New Features
  - Domain Health Row — three live status cards above the dashboard tab switcher (Data Protection, Cybersecurity, Risk Management); each card switches to the corresponding tab
  - Dashboard KPI row: IAP card now shows non-compliant member count, colour-coded variant (amber/red), and links to IAP admin
  - Needs Attention panel items deep-link directly to the individual task
  - TIA "at risk" badge in the dashboard TeamAssessment header; shows count of non-authorised transfers or "✓ All permitted"
  - Webhooks table: new "Last delivery" column showing most recent Svix attempt status and timestamp (success / pending / failed)
- Enhancements
  - Direction B design language applied across all modules — unified card shell, panel headers, table header typography, tab bar, and hover states (All Tasks, RPA, TIA, PIA, CSC, RM, IAP, Dashboard)
  - Module Create buttons and empty-state CTAs migrated from DaisyUI to Shadcn `<Button>`
  - `ModuleBadge` rewritten as a pure Tailwind component; rendered inline in All Tasks and the Dashboard task matrix
  - Module page headings with record count pill added to RPA, TIA, PIA, RM, and IAP
  - Comments redesign: single-column layout, hover-reveal edit/delete, Direction B typography
  - IAP completion summary banner above the course grid
  - RM table: replaced unreadable rotated `VerticalHeader` with a two-row grouped header (Raw Risk / Treatment / Target Risk / Current Risk)
  - CSC: `StatusesTable` + `SectionRail` wrapped in a single Direction B card; `SectionRail` hidden below `lg:` breakpoint
  - All table action columns standardised to icon-only buttons with `aria-label` (Tasks, RPA, TIA, PIA, RM, Members, Invitations, IAP admin, Webhooks)
  - TIA country fields now display translated country names (was rendering raw lowercase stored keys)
  - `AuditTimeline` generic component wired to all modules (RPA, TIA, PIA, CSC, RM)
  - Removed leftover debug labels in RmAnalysis and TeamCscAnalysis
- Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)
  - `<html lang>` attribute set from SSR locale on every page
  - All Chart.js canvases wrapped in `role="img"` containers with descriptive `aria-label`
  - Mobile sidebar (`Drawer`) rewritten as an accessible dialog: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, focus-on-open, Escape key, Tab focus trap, `aria-hidden` backdrop
  - Dashboard tab bar wired with full ARIA tab pattern (`tablist`, `tab`, `tabpanel`)
  - Notification bell `aria-label` is dynamic with unread count; badge carries `aria-hidden`
  - Webhook form: events fieldset wrapped in `<fieldset><legend>`; inputs wired with `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, and `role="alert"` error messages
  - All icon-only buttons and interactive cards carry `aria-label`; active domain health cards carry `aria-pressed`
  - External navigation links include `<span class="sr-only">(opens in new tab)</span>`
  - Content text colour raised from `text-slate-400` to `text-slate-500` across KPI strip, task analysis, risk analysis, and webhooks table to meet 4.5:1 contrast ratio
- Billing
  - Pricing page redesign — "Most Popular" badge on Premium, plan descriptions, green module checkmarks, blue feature checkmarks, bottom upgrade nudge
  - Monthly / Annual billing toggle with 20% discount on annual plans (Premium: €15.20/mo · €182.40/yr; Ultimate: €39.20/mo · €470.40/yr)
  - Annual billing stored on subscription (`isAnnual` field); next invoice date advances 12 months instead of 1
  - Payment card reflects annual discount on price-per-user and total; shows "/yr" billing cycle and "Annual" badge
  - Post-request toast now shows a friendly confirmation message in all 7 languages
- Mobile & Responsive
  - Teams table: added `overflow-x-auto` inner wrapper so the table scrolls horizontally on small screens instead of clipping
  - Risk matrix chart: wrapped in `overflow-x-auto` to allow horizontal scrolling on mobile
  - All Tasks toolbar: fixed conflicting `items-end`/`items-center` classes; toolbar now stacks vertically on mobile and aligns inline on `lg:+`
  - Task filter dropdowns: each filter gets `flex-1 min-w-[150px]` so the three selectors share available width evenly on narrow viewports
  - All remaining tables audited against the nested two-div overflow pattern (`overflow-hidden rounded-xl` outer / `overflow-x-auto` inner)
- Translations & Internationalisation
  - **Italian, Japanese, and Portuguese added as fully supported locales** — 880+ keys translated per language across all modules (Tasks, RPA, TIA, PIA, CSC, RM, IAP, Dashboard, Settings, Fleet, Auth)
  - Language switcher (`UpdateLanguage` card) added to Profile → Account settings; all 7 locales are now selectable in-app without touching the URL
  - `next-i18next.config.js` updated to register `it`, `ja`, `pt`; `localeLabels.ts` extended with native-script names (Italiano, 日本語, Português)
  - Missing namespace files created for IT, JA, PT: `rm.json` (risk table headers, field/form labels), `rpa.json`, `tia.json`, `pia.json` (full PIA risk-level descriptions, step labels, field names), and `iap.json` (completion-progress, total-courses, completed, in-progress)
  - `iap.json` namespace created for all 7 locales and wired into `serverSideTranslations` on the IAP index and admin pages — dashboard labels ("Your completion", "Total", "Completed", "In progress") now translate correctly
  - Hardcoded English labels removed from components and replaced with `t()` calls:
    - `CscStatusBadge` — status labels now resolve via `t('statuses.{status}.label')` (uses the same nested key as the CSC pie chart)
    - `CompletionResultsChart` — chart labels now use `t('progress.todo/inprogress/done')`
    - `StatusResultsChart` — chart labels now use `t('passed')` / `t('failed')`
  - All nested translation objects in `common.json` translated for IT, JA, PT: `statuses` (CSC maturity labels + descriptions), `task-statuses`, `task-priorities`, `chart-risk-impact`, `chart-risk-probability`, `chart-risk-axis`, `progress`, `errors`, `settings-tabs`, `recurrence-presets`, `recurrence-units`, `recurrence-unit-options`, `task-recurrence-statuses`, `soa-export`, `csc-mapping`, `csc-status-prompt`, `notifications`, `sso`
  - Added 30+ missing flat keys across all 7 locales: `section-progress`, `status-distribution`, `risk-matrix-axis-label`, `pia-matrix-axis`, `top-open-risks`, `framework`, 18× `domain-health.*` keys (card titles, tab-switch aria-labels, metric strings), `chart.task-status-distribution-aria-label`, `dashboard.kpi.yet-to-complete`, `tia-at-risk`, `tia-all-permitted`, `tia-non-adequate-warning`, `success-message`, `change-language`
  - Dashboard task matrix column headers migrated from hardcoded English strings to `task-statuses.*` i18n keys
  - Domain health card tab-switch aria-labels (`Switch to Data Protection / Cybersecurity / Risk Management tab`) now fully translated
  - CSC bulk-action toast messages split into distinct keys (`csc.bulk-status-updated`, `csc.bulk-tasks-linked`) with proper `{{count}}` / `{{status}}` interpolation
- API
  - `PUT /api/teams/{slug}/csc` (single control status update) added to OpenAPI spec — was previously undocumented; `public/openapi.json` regenerated
- Testing
  - 62 Jest unit and API handler tests added: status-key regression guard, CSC helper invariants, dashboard counting logic, full CRUD coverage for `/tasks` and `/tasks/[taskNumber]`, and both CSC endpoints
  - 3 Playwright E2E test suites added: dashboard task matrix + tab switching, task list / kanban usability, CSC bulk status change and task assignment
- Fixes
  - TIA: Legal Analysis column was rendering `DataExporter` instead of `LawImporterCountry`
  - PIA: First column header was labelled with the wrong translation key
  - CSC: Dark mode inactive tabs appeared selected due to unconditional `dark:text-slate-200`
  - RM: Asset Owner column showed "Not found" due to invalid Map bracket access; fixed to `.get()`
  - RM: Unstable row keys (`key={idx}`) changed to `key={task.id}`
  - CSC: Bulk status change was updating only the last selected control — root cause was `mutateStatuses()` called after every individual write, causing SWR re-fetches to race with Prisma's read-modify-write on the JSON blob; fixed by writing all controls first, then mutating once
  - CSC: Task assignment required a full page refresh to appear — `useTeamTasks.mutateTasks` called `mutate(url)` without `await` (fire-and-forget); fixed by adding `await`
  - Dashboard: Task matrix status counters showed 0 for In Progress and In Review — `STATUS_COLS` keys used `in-progress`/`in-review` instead of the DB-stored `inprogress`/`inreview`; fixed across dashboard, `TeamTasksAnalysis`, `GlobalSearch`, and `TaskKanbanBoard`

